.TH LIUXIN 1 "2026-11-02" "LiuXin-alpha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
liuxin \- manage a LiuXin catalogue, storage and workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B liuxin
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B liuxin init
.I SYSTEM_ROOT
.br
.B liuxin
.I command
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
LiuXin provides named commands for catalogue operations, managed storage,
metadata and acquisition workflows.
Use
.B liuxin \-\-help
to list command families and a family's
.B \-\-help
to inspect its current subcommands.
.PP
For remote-file registration and optional downloads, see
.BR liuxin-ingest-web (1).
For the distinction between web and local-file ingest, see
.BR liuxin-ingest (1).
.SH CONNECTION SELECTION
Core-backed commands accept one of
.BR \-\-system-root " " DIRECTORY ,
.BR \-\-profile " " PROFILE ,
.BR \-\-database " " PATH ,
or
.BR \-\-core-endpoint " " URL .
A saved connection from
.B liuxin connect
can supply the default. Explicit selectors take precedence over environment
selectors and saved connections.
.PP
.B \-\-core-token-file PATH
supplies a remote Core bearer token.
Remote web-ingest execution requires trusted Core authority.
Local filesystem paths used by managed workflows belong to the Core host;
CLI output files belong to the CLI host.
.SH MAINTENANCE
.B liuxin maintenance install
explicitly installs catalogue change capture and required Work revision plugins.
Mutation commands preview unless
.B \-\-yes
is supplied. Prompt work succeeds in the source transaction or rolls that write back.
Lazy work remains durable until a worker completes it.
.PP
.B maintenance status
reports pending work, attempts and errors without starting a worker.
.B maintenance drain
runs bounded maintenance job passes; queued storage audits are left for the
normal jobs worker. Repeat it for continued progress.
Use
.B maintenance retry PLUGIN
to reset failed work,
.B maintenance pause PLUGIN
and
.B maintenance resume PLUGIN
to control delivery, and
.B maintenance prune
to remove fully acknowledged journal records.
Pausing a required prompt plugin blocks its source writes.
Queued lazy deliveries encountered while paused retain their obligations and
retry budget; resume publishes fresh deliveries. Use maintenance retry for these
jobs; generic Core jobs retry refuses them before creating a successor.
.PP
.B maintenance prune-jobs
retires completed maintenance job history after checking the current catalogue
journal. Preview is the default; pass
.B \-\-yes
to apply. The default
.B \-\-older-than-days
is 7 (0 explicitly permits immediate retirement).
.B \-\-max-events
bounds the inspected page to 1 through 500 runs, default 128. When has_more is
true, continue with
.B \-\-before-run-id
set to next_before_run_id. Pending obligations, active work, retained retry
successors and unrelated jobs remain protected. Approved runs, events, request
keys and unused definitions are removed; retired job IDs cease to be inspectable
or retryable. Freed SQLite pages are reusable; no VACUUM is performed.
.PP
.B maintenance rebuild
backfills or repairs Work projection receipts and expression counts, resuming a
saved cursor. Each page scans at most
.B \-\-max-events
identities (1 to 500), with
.B \-\-max-batches
pages per invocation (1 to 128, default 1).
Pass
.B \-\-yes
to schedule work and
.B \-\-restart
to begin a fresh scan. Bibliographic rows and files are unchanged. Derived values
are invalidated page by page, including stale keys for deleted Works.
Repeat until scheduling_complete, then drain lazy work. Status distinguishes
source/projection scanning, waiting for delivery, and completed rebuilds.
.PP
.B maintenance upgrade PLUGIN \-\-from-version VERSION
reads an implementation-authored upgrade plan. Pass
.B \-\-yes
to apply, optionally with
.B \-\-expected-definition HASH
from the preview. Apply rechecks the installed version under the writer lock.
Pending work must drain with its old implementation unless the new plugin
explicitly supports replay; dependent work and mode changes require draining.
The migration invalidates affected projections and fences old jobs atomically.
Run the owner's rebuild afterward; an obsolete Work rebuild needs
.BR \-\-restart .
Status retains the latest upgrade receipt for each plugin.
.PP
.B maintenance duplicates TABLE COLUMN
reports duplicate candidates without changing rows or starting a worker.
Results contain value, scope and row_ids; only repeated nonblank text is returned.
The default
.B \-\-comparison identity
uses declared normalization, or NFKC/whitespace/casefold for undeclared text.
Other modes are nocase (NFC/casefold) and exact (stored text).
Declared identity scopes apply to every mode. Equal titles do not prove entity identity.
.B \-\-max-rows
bounds a complete scan (default 10000, maximum 100000); oversized selections fail
with scan_limit_exceeded rather than returning incomplete groups.
.B \-\-where-file PATH
reads a JSON object of physical-column equality filters.
Automatic duplicate consolidation is unavailable.
.PP
.B maintenance clean
is unavailable in the built-in service and returns capability_unavailable without
deleting rows.
.B maintenance merge
transfers registered interlinks and deletes the absorbed row in one transaction.
Conflicting duplicate link payloads or write failures roll back the operation.
It does not combine scalar metadata, intralinks or tree relationships.
.PP
For example:
.nf
liuxin maintenance install \-\-database catalog.sqlite \-\-yes
liuxin maintenance drain \-\-database catalog.sqlite \-\-yes
liuxin maintenance status \-\-database catalog.sqlite
.fi
.SH AGENT NAME MAINTENANCE
.B catalog agents rename ID NAME
changes an Agent's canonical name and sort value atomically.
.B catalog agents repair-sort ID [ID ...]
repairs sorts for 1 to 500 explicit IDs without changing canonical names.
Both commands preview unless
.B \-\-yes
is supplied; no maintenance installation or worker is required.
.PP
.B \-\-sort-mode preserve
is the default: retain nonblank stored sorts and derive missing ones.
.B \-\-sort-mode derive
explicitly regenerates existing sorts. Rename also accepts
.B \-\-sort-name TEXT
as a nonblank override, incompatible with derive.
.B \-\-person-sort-method
accepts comma (default), nocomma, or copy. Organisations, groups and pseudonyms
retain display order. Locale is not inferred; use copy or an explicit override
where person-name inversion is inappropriate.
.PP
Aliases, subtype details and credits are preserved. Invalid rows or write failures
roll back the complete operation. Applying rereads current values under locks;
a preview is advisory.
.SH CATALOG REPAIR
.B catalog inherited-tags LEVEL ID
reads direct and inherited tags with every WEMI relationship path and source
identity retained. It does not copy metadata or start a worker.
.B \-\-max-rows
bounds the complete inspection; exceeding the budget refuses a partial result.
.PP
.B catalog repair merge REQUEST.json
and
.B catalog repair cleanup REQUEST.json
preview explicit JSON identity/conflict or discard/preserve decisions.
Apply requires
.B \-\-yes \-\-expected-state HASH
using the inspected preview's state. Changed references, unsupported ownership
or unresolved conflicts refuse the whole repair. Changes and their audit receipt
commit together. Neither operation changes physical files.
.PP
.B catalog repair receipt ID
reads a durable receipt without installing storage. The existing
.B catalog metadata merge LEVEL SOURCE TARGET
also previews by default and requires the same apply flags. It accepts
.B \-\-resolutions-file
and
.B \-\-relationship-resolutions-file
for explicit decisions; silent target precedence is removed.
.SH OUTPUT
Operational commands return JSON. Use
.B \-\-compact
for compact JSON and
.B \-\-output PATH
for a CLI-host output file.
.B \-\-replace-output
permits replacement of an existing output file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
liuxin init "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin storage status \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web https://example.org/books/ \e
  \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web \-\-help
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIUXIN_SYSTEM_ROOT
Select a system root when no explicit selector is supplied.
.TP
.B LIUXIN_PROFILE
Select a configured profile.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Parent of LiuXin's profile and saved-connection configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR liuxin-ingest (1),
.BR liuxin-ingest-web (1)
.PP
The source checkout contains user guides in
.B docs/
and implementation documentation in
